  "generated_text": "To find the greatest product obtainable from two integers whose sum is 1998, we can use the concept of symmetry. Let's denote the two integers by \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) such that \\(a + b = 1998\\). We want to maximize the product \\(ab\\).\n\nFirst, we note that the product \\(ab\\) is maximized when \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are as close to each other as possible. This is because the product of two numbers is maximized when the numbers are equal or as equal as possible. Therefore, we should choose \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) to be as close to each other as possible.\n\nSince 1998 is an even number, we can split it into two equal parts. Thus, we set \\(a = 999\\) and \\(b = 999\\).\n\nNow, we calculate the product \\(ab\\):\n\\[\nab = 999 \\times 999 = 998001\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the greatest product obtainable from two integers whose sum is 1998 is \\(\\boxed{998001}\\).",
  "grade": {
